# Byte fidelity for the S6 publish gate.
#
# This repository contains ONLY the gated production build. Every file here was
# hashed after the QA gate passed, and the live site is verified byte-identical
# against those hashes. Any line-ending normalisation between commit and
# checkout would silently change the hash of every text asset - the JS bundle,
# the CSS, index.html - and the live byte-identity check would then fail on
# files that are in fact correct, or pass on files that are not.
#
# `* -text` disables ALL text conversion: git stores and checks out exactly the
# bytes it was given. Combined with `core.autocrlf false` this makes the tree
# hash recorded in docs/publish/PUBLISH.md a meaningful contract.
* -text
